+
+## Local harness (ron-skills overlay)
+
+These lines override the rest of this skill and its playbooks on this machine.
+
+- **Claude Code names.** Read `~/code/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md` once per session and map Cursor tools, subagent fields, models, paths, and Cursor-only steps with it. Where it and these lines differ, these lines win; read its `<pstack>/skills/<name>` as `~/.claude/skills/<name>`.
+- **Repo rules win.** The repo's `AGENTS.md` and adapter docs outrank any pstack step, including language: user-visible text, comments, commit messages, and tracker notes follow the repo's language rule. **Writing the reply** and **Comments** apply only where they do not conflict.
+- **Forge.** There are no GitHub PRs. A delivery unit is a local branch with a candidate commit; "PR", "stack", "merge-ready", and "land" map to the repo adapter's candidate, batch branch, regression, and local merge into the integration branch. Push only as the adapter grants. Skip `gh`, `origin`, `watch-pr`, Babysit, Shipping, and Opening a PR.
+- **No cloud.** A delivery unit that would be `environment: "cloud"` runs as one Orca terminal session in its own worktree, dispatched by the repo's tooling, not as an `isolation: "worktree"` subagent. Docker test runs share the machine, so respect the concurrency cap in the standing orders.
+- **Models.** Two families: Claude subagents (`model` plus `effort`) and Codex through the repo's Codex runner or review script. Every non-Claude slug, `grok-*` included, means Codex. When Codex fails, fall back to the `code-review` skill and record that verdict as lower-grade.
+- **Linked set.** `~/code/ron-skills/pstack-skills.txt` lists what is linked; `arena` carries its own local overlay and `eval` runs through it. pstack's `tdd` and `teach` are replaced by Matt's. Where a trigger names an unlinked skill, use the Matt equivalent (`grilling`, `codebase-design`, `tdd`, `code-review`, `diagnosing-bugs`) or skip it with a one-line reason. Do not install or run `scripts/` (bun, watch-pr).
 
